build: 2026-06-23 v10.58.0 (rPPG lock fix — autocorrelation seed + stage telemetry)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: Device run (founder, on hardware) showed the audio pipeline healthy (13 notes generate, pattern ticks, synth noteOn fires) but rPPG never locked a heart rate: finger=yes, signal quality plateaued at q≈0.30, yet bpm=0 conf=0.00 for the whole session. Root cause found in CameraAnalyzer.detectPeaks: the FRESH-LOCK corroboration gate (estimatedBPM==0 path) DISCARDED any window where discrete peak-counting disagreed >20% with a confident autocorrelation period — so when peak-counting kept catching a dicrotic notch / harmonic, the BPM never seeded ("bpm=0 forever"). FIX: on that disagreement, SEED from the robust autocorrelation period (the more reliable periodicity estimate) instead of returning empty-handed; normal tracking resumes next window. Autocorrelation is now computed once per scan and reused for the fresh-lock check, the few-peaks fallback, and telemetry. TELEMETRY: the device breadcrumb now logs amp (filtered pulse amplitude), pk (peak count), and acf (autocorrelation strength) alongside finger/R/bright/q/bpm/conf, so the next on-device run pinpoints exactly which stage blocks a lock (amp≈0 → no pulsatile AC / press lighter; pk<3 + high acf → rounded waveform, now seeded; acf low → genuinely weak perfusion). 2 code files (CameraAnalyzer, CameraRPPGBioPublisher); PulsePeriodEstimator unchanged. Compile-gate validates; behaviour is device-verified on the founder's next run.
